cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use convinterp in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "convinterp: high-order convolution interpolation, derivatives and integrals on uniform grids"
authors:
  - given-names: Nikolaj Maack
    family-names: Bielefeld
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4385-6444"
abstract: >-
  convinterp interpolates data on uniform grids in any number of dimensions, and differentiates
  and integrates the interpolant exactly, with piecewise-polynomial convolution kernels of up to
  7th-order accuracy, evaluated in a compiled Rust core. It is a port of the Julia package
  ConvolutionInterpolations.jl by the same author, and is tested against it.
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-26
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22972816"
url: "https://convinterp.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NikoBiele/convinterp"
keywords:
  - interpolation
  - convolution
  - derivatives
  - integration
  - numerical methods
  - scientific computing